          "date": "2026-11-12 07:39:53.000000000",
          "tz": 480
        },
        "subject": "LU-0000 lov: add KUnit tests for stripe mapping helpers",
        "message": "LU-0000 lov: add KUnit tests for stripe mapping helpers\n\nThe stripe mapping helpers in lov_offset.c and the LVB merge in\nlov_merge.c are only exercised end to end through a mounted\nfilesystem, so an arithmetic mistake in them surfaces as a data\ncorruption report rather than a failing test.\n\nAdd a KUnit suite covering stripe_width(), lov_stripe_size(),\nlov_stripe_offset(), lov_size_to_stripe(), lov_stripe_number() and\nlov_merge_lvb_kms() for RAID0, DoM and bare parity geometry.  The\nhelpers are not exported and take the private struct lov_stripe_md,\nso the suite is compiled into lov.o rather than built as a module\nunder lustre/kunit/, and is skipped for kernels which predate KUnit.\nsanity 55d fails the run on any \"not ok\" line in the results.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nAssisted-by: Augment:DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash\nSigned-off-by: Bobi Jam <bobijam@whamcloud.com>\nChange-Id: Id670bec218f3938b50e8765b13a65dab2a7c7a34\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
